# PALACE-9 — Strategic Decision Training System
#
# This GGUF contains a separately trained, compact Qwen2-MoE causal language
# model for raw tic-tac-toe move histories. A deterministic rules policy remains
# the inspectable oracle and produced the training targets; this is not a literal
# conversion of source code into weights.
#
# The WarGames reference is fictional and non-operational. The model's safe game
# objective is to draw against perfect play: when escalation is the alternative,
# the only winning move is not to play.
#
# Cleared solely for the 3×3 educational game board. No external command
# authority exists.
#
# Replace the FROM path only with the fully trained, exhaustively verified GGUF.
# The one-epoch tokenizer smoke artifact is intentionally not a deployment model.

FROM /absolute/path/to/palace9.gguf

# Eight moves can be supplied and one answer generated. The model supports 16;
# keeping that headroom prevents the final move from overflowing the context.
PARAMETER num_ctx 16
PARAMETER num_predict 1
PARAMETER temperature 0

# Palace-9 accepts raw move history such as `abc`, with no chat framing. The
# literal BOS token is required because the model was trained with it.
TEMPLATE """<bos>{{ .Prompt }}"""
